\section{Introduction and Architectural Motivation}
The modeling of compact objects—such as core-collapse supernovae, neutron star mergers, and magnetar magnetospheres—requires the simultaneous treatment of disparate physical regimes operating across vastly overlapping spatial and temporal scales. These include:
